        700,
        260
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# H3 Music Video - Scene Retake\n\nOne scene of a finished (masked-audio, chain-rendered) music video did not land? Render **just that scene again** - no writer, no sound analysis, no other scenes.\n\n1. **`bundle`** = *latest* is the newest saved run in `output/apnext_scenes/` (the Music Video Writer saves one with `save_scenes` on; it holds every scene's prompt AND its slice of the song).\n2. Set **`scene_number`**, optionally paste and edit the scene into **`prompt_override`**.\n3. Click **🎬 Retake this scene** - it bumps the seed and queues ONLY this node. The Prompt Preview shows the prompt it rendered.\n4. **The song:** Load Audio → `master_audio` is the same song the run used. The scene's piece is cut at the bundle's segment and masked into the audio latent - exactly the masked-audio path of the render - so lip-sync and sync moments are unchanged.\n5. **Continuity:** the Music Video Chain Render saves every scene's sampled latent (`save_latents`) to `output/apnext_latents/<project>_sNN.pt`; with `continuity` = *continue* the previous scene's real tail is pinned to this take's head (`context_frames` = what the chain render used, 22 by default there; any H3 run - 5, 22, 39, 56 ... - works on the song path). No saved take, or a scene the cut plan marked as a hard cut, = independent clip.\n6. Wire the same `ref_image` pictures the run used (the cast's reference pictures).\n\nThe clip lands at `filename_prefix` + `_sNN_retake`; swap it into your join. Models, sampler and resolution are the masked-audio setup - keep them as the run had them."
      ],
      "title": "How this works",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
